Subject: [PATCH RFC 0/4] HID: spi-hid: P16 reset and report-transaction fixes

This draft fixes GPIO IRQ lookup, ACPI reset dispatch and GET-report
transactions, and adds a stream-only input quirk for the P16 sensor hub.

The base is HID for-next commit 720806515cb6921ab05caaa6f470f7054b56385e.
That base does not contain the SPI HID driver. The review branch imports
the pinned June 9 SPI HID series, the coherent RX support in the SPI core,
and the SPI HID portion of the Surface Pro 11 support patch. The latter
two imports are limited to the SPI core, SPI HID and its input binding;
no unrelated platform changes are included.

Fixes tags name commits in this local prerequisite stack. They must be
remapped when the maintainer selects the actual prerequisite branch.
The prerequisite-patch-id trailers identify the tested imported stack.

Validation:
- Full ARM64 vmlinux and module links with both ACPI and OF frontends.
- Each of the four commits builds independently in that configuration.
- Full ARM64 built-in OF link with ACPI, DMI, PM and modules disabled.
- No SPI HID compiler warnings. Minimal kernel builds have pre-existing
  ARM64, proc, block and library warnings (526 warning lines in each
  configuration, identical to the prerequisite baseline).
- ASan/UBSan tests of the actual request/transport callbacks, including
  deterministic concurrent raw requests. The baseline returns caller 2's
  bytes to caller 1; the fixed callbacks preserve both complete replies.
- Five installed-kernel header builds and 124 platform tests pass.

The target kernel has not been booted on the P16. The installed transport
has already provided live IIO readings with these functional fixes; the
reset diagnostic has since been reduced to debug level. Other SPI HID
hardware and runtime lockdep on this target stack are untested.

Tool assistance: OpenAI Codex inspected and split the local adaptations,
reviewed dependencies, adjusted reset logging, wrote the concurrency
reproducer and test/build orchestration, and prepared these draft messages.
Human review and a human DCO sign-off remain required. No sign-off or
review tag is asserted for these four commits.

Johann-Peter Hartmann (4):
  HID: spi-hid: retry ACPI GPIO IRQ lookup at probe
  HID: spi-hid: evaluate reset on the ACPI handle
  HID: spi-hid: serialize and type GET report responses
  HID: spi-hid: handle P16 stream-only input reports

